WEBVTT
NOTE Cedwyn film, frame 011, en. Timings estimated from the script until the clip is rendered (re-split 27 Oct 2026: <=2x42 chars, <=20 cps, <=180 wpm).

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.333
<v Nia>Eighteen seventy-six. Thirty-three acres
go to the limeworks. Whose land was it?

2
00:00:05.753 --> 00:00:11.020
<v Gwen>[in Welsh] Bore da! Worrall's Directory
of South Wales, off the carrier's cart.

3
00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:14.873
<v Gwen>Here, Llandough parish,
Penarth section: 'Williams John,

4
00:00:14.993 --> 00:00:17.593
<v Gwen>Great house.' In print for all Cardiff.

5
00:00:18.013 --> 00:00:21.680
<v the Bute estate agent>A directory prints whoever
answers the canvasser, Gwen.

6
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:24.267
<v the Bute estate agent>It puts John Williams at Great House.

7
00:00:24.387 --> 00:00:27.194
<v the Bute estate agent>It doesn't tell you who owns the place.

8
00:00:27.614 --> 00:00:31.747
<v Gwen>Slater's had him there in
sixty-eight too, mind. And the land?

9
00:00:31.867 --> 00:00:36.078
<v Gwen>The Marquess is lord of the manor,
same as half this parish.

10
00:00:36.498 --> 00:00:38.252
<v the Bute estate agent>Lord of the manor, yes.

11
00:00:38.372 --> 00:00:42.239
<v the Bute estate agent>Whose freehold this ground is,
a directory can't tell you.

12
00:00:42.359 --> 00:00:45.759
<v the Bute estate agent>And his lordship's business
today is the limeworks.

13
00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:49.479
<v the Bute estate agent>Thirty-three acres, formerly
part of Great House Farm,

14
00:00:49.599 --> 00:00:51.465
<v the Bute estate agent>for the Llandough Limeworks.

15
00:00:51.585 --> 00:00:55.919
<v the Bute estate agent>The plan's drawn and engrossed on
the deeds at the estate office.

16
00:00:56.339 --> 00:01:00.539
<v Gwen>Daniel Thomas and Son's kiln and
quarry are down there already.

17
00:01:00.959 --> 00:01:04.492
<v the Bute estate agent>Which brings me to the poor
rate. October, Llandough.

18
00:01:04.612 --> 00:01:08.745
<v the Bute estate agent>John Williams, farm, owner Lord
Bute, about seventy-six acres,

19
00:01:08.865 --> 00:01:11.532
<v the Bute estate agent>gross forty-one pounds nought shillings.

20
00:01:11.652 --> 00:01:16.785
<v the Bute estate agent>Lord Bute, woods in hand, thirty-two
acres, three roods, thirty-nine perches.

21
00:01:16.905 --> 00:01:19.839
<v the Bute estate agent>Daniel Thomas and Son,
lime kiln and quarry.

22
00:01:20.259 --> 00:01:25.392
<v Gwen>So John's charged for seventy-six acres,
and the limeworks gets thirty-three.

23
00:01:25.512 --> 00:01:29.372
<v Gwen>Does your book make him a
tenant? Yearly? On a lease?

24
00:01:29.792 --> 00:01:32.925
<v the Bute estate agent>It makes him the occupier
the overseers charge.

25
00:01:33.045 --> 00:01:36.645
<v the Bute estate agent>How he holds is the estate's
affair, not the parish's.

26
00:01:41.065 --> 00:01:42.732
<v Nia>Worrall's 1875, page 324,

27
00:01:42.852 --> 00:01:46.918
<v Nia>digitised by the University of
Leicester Special Collections:

28
00:01:47.038 --> 00:01:50.505
<v Nia>a Williams farmer at 'Great
house', Penarth section.

29
00:01:50.625 --> 00:01:55.692
<v Nia>The Legal Wiki follows him on: Slater's
1868 and 1880, Owen's 1887 and 1891,

30
00:01:55.812 --> 00:01:58.945
<v Nia>the 1901 Cardiff Directory,
all at Great House.

31
00:01:59.065 --> 00:02:02.574
<v Nia>A listing shows where he
lived, not who held title.

32
00:02:02.994 --> 00:02:07.860
<v Nia>The National Library of Wales catalogue
for Bute deeds D153/4 to 8 reads:

33
00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:11.247
<v Nia>'land (33 a.), formerly
part of Great House Farm,

34
00:02:11.367 --> 00:02:13.767
<v Nia>for the Llandough Limeworks (33 a.),

35
00:02:13.887 --> 00:02:16.754
<v Nia>1876-1912.' Plan
engrossed on D153/3, 1875,

36
00:02:16.874 --> 00:02:18.174
<v Nia>and 4, 1876.

37
00:02:18.294 --> 00:02:22.894
<v Nia>The deeds, their parties, the exact
parcel: we haven't read them yet.

38
00:02:23.314 --> 00:02:24.717
<v Nia>And the rate book:

39
00:02:24.837 --> 00:02:29.171
<v Nia>the same sequence of names appears
in a rate of twentieth August,

40
00:02:29.291 --> 00:02:31.091
<v Nia>eighteen-seventy-something.

41
00:02:31.211 --> 00:02:33.316
<v Nia>The last figure can't be read.

42
00:02:33.436 --> 00:02:35.892
<v Nia>It shows who was charged, for what.

43
00:02:36.012 --> 00:02:37.766
<v Nia>It doesn't show a lease.
